<description>
Extract the largest clean framed sprite whose foreground pattern is not duplicated.

Input structure
- The grid has one dominant background color and two foreground colors.
- The foreground contains several same-size rectangular sprites with a one-cell frame.
- Extra foreground clutter may touch the outside of a sprite, and smaller framed subpatterns may occur inside repeated sprites.

Rule
- Find clean rectangles whose border is one foreground color and whose interior contains no background.
- Keep only the largest such rectangles; these are the full source sprites.
- Among those sprites, return the single full sprite pattern that occurs exactly once.

Key insight
The surrounding clutter is irrelevant once the maximal intact frames are detected; the task is an odd-one-out selection among the clean sprite patterns.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "maximal clean one-cell framed rectangular sprites on the dominant background, ignoring attached foreground clutter and smaller nested frames",
  "transform": "select the single maximal sprite pattern that occurs exactly once among the same-size framed sprites and output that sprite unchanged",
  "grid_shape": "height and width of the selected framed sprite crop"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  colors:
    bg: any single color, most frequent (~50-65% of grid)
    frame_color: one fg color, forms sprite borders and clutter
    fill_color: second fg color, appears only inside sprite interiors
  grid: 16-18 rows x 16-18 cols (square)
  sprites:
    count: 3-5 same-size framed rectangles, non-overlapping
    size: 4x4 or 5x5 (1-cell frame_color border, 2x2 or 3x3 interior)
    interior: mix of frame_color and fill_color cells, no bg; fill_color >=2 cells
    patterns: exactly 2 distinct interior patterns; one repeated (N-1 times), one unique (1 time)
    unique_differs_from_repeated: some interior cells swap between frame_color and fill_color
    gap_between_sprites: >=1 cell (no touching borders)
  clutter:
    scattered single frame_color cells and small clusters (1-3 cells) on bg
    density: ~9-14% of grid cells
    fill_color never appears outside sprites
    some clutter cells adjacent to sprite borders, some isolated
  output: the unique sprite (entire framed rectangle including border), cropped

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 3 colors (bg, frame_color, fill_color). Pick sprite size S in {4,5} and count N in {3,4,5}.
    2. Generate two distinct SxS sprite patterns (all-frame_color border, interior mixes frame_color+fill_color, no bg, >=2 fill cells).
    3. Designate one as REPEATED (placed N-1 times) and the other as UNIQUE (placed once). Output = UNIQUE.
    4. Choose grid size (16-18, square) large enough to fit N non-overlapping sprites with >=1 cell gap. Place sprites at random non-overlapping positions.
    5. Fill remaining cells with bg, then scatter ~10-14% clutter (frame_color only) as isolated cells and small clusters across bg areas.
    6. Verify: no accidental new framed rects formed by clutter; all N intended sprites are cleanly detectable.
```
